Package: raye-gaming
Architecture: all
Depends: raye-windows-apps, winetricks, cabextract,
         gamemode, mangohud, gamescope, vulkan-tools,
         steam-devices | steam-launcher, libgdk-pixbuf-2.0-0,
         raye-scx,
         raye-proton,
         ${misc:Depends}
# raye-proton: Steam's compatibility tool built by Raye from GE-Proton
# (packages/raye-proton); it used to be a launcher shipped here.
# Valve's own Steam .deb (steam-launcher) conflicts with steam-devices and
# brings the same rules itself: either one is fine, so installing it only
# swaps the two (release/gaming/tests/test_third_party_debs.py).
# Minecraft's official .deb still depends on the library's pre-24.04 name,
# which no package has anymore, so it could not be installed at all.
Provides: libgdk-pixbuf2.0-0 (= 2.44.5)
Description: Raye Linux games and Windows apps
 Raye's layer for Windows programs, with the kernel's ntsync for games,
 GameMode to give games the whole machine while they run, MangoHud for
 the frame rate overlay, gamescope for upscaling. Steam
 and the game launchers are offered in the Store, they come with their
 own licence.

Package: raye-windows-apps
Architecture: all
Depends: raye-wine, raye-wine-compat | wine, raye-windows-ui, winetricks, cabextract, unzip, zstd, kdialog, util-linux, xvfb, xauth,
         libnotify-bin,
         fonts-liberation, fonts-crosextra-carlito,
         fonts-crosextra-caladea,
         osslsigncode, kio-extras,
# raye-wine-compat gives winetricks the "wine" it asks for; a system that
# still has WineHQ's package keeps it rather than an update removing it.
# raye-wine-addons is not needed: raye-wine brings Mono, Gecko, DXVK and
# vkd3d-proton itself. Drop kdialog above once SW-11's runner lands.
         ${misc:Depends}
Description: Open Windows programs with a double click
 Double-clicking an .exe or .msi file opens it, each program in
 its own space so one cannot break the others. Every space starts from a
 ready one, prepared in the background after login with the pieces most
 programs and games expect (core fonts, DXVK, vkd3d-proton),
 so a program opens at once and nothing asks a question.

Package: raye-kernel
Architecture: all
Depends: mokutil, shim-signed, ${misc:Depends}
Description: Switch to the Raye kernel safely
 The Raye kernel is Ubuntu's kernel with the Raye crash screen, signed
 with the Raye key. This package holds the public key and the steps
 that enroll it before the kernel is installed, so Secure Boot never
 meets a kernel it does not know. Ubuntu's signed kernel stays as the
 fallback.
